              skills/nehr-data-mapping/references/nhdd-samples/*.json (NHDD)
  Generated:  2026-05-05  (revision 4 — all-fields-filled reference)

  PURPOSE
  =================
  A teaching reference, not a transmittable message. Shows every populatable
  element of putEvent filled with a realistic example value, plus annotations
  about Significance, Cardinality, Data Type/Length, and a "what to fill" note.

  Use this to learn the shape of each element. For real transmissions, refer to
  NEHR_putEvent_Sample_Heart_Clinic.xml (single patient, outpatient cardiology).

  DELIBERATE INCONSISTENCY NOTE
  =================
  Real putEvent messages are EITHER outpatient (eventType=4) OR inpatient
  (eventType=1 or 2). This file shows BOTH patterns for reference — the
  inpatient-only elements (admittingClinician, dischargingClinician,
  dischargeInformation) are clearly tagged "INPATIENT ONLY" and must NOT be
  emitted in an outpatient message. For Heart Clinic (outpatient cardiology),
  omit those entirely.

  ANNOTATION FORMAT
  =================
  <element>VALUE</element>  <! [SIG] card N..N TypeName(MaxLen) | meaning >

    Significance:  M = Mandatory, O = Optional, C = Conditional Mandatory
    Cardinality:   1 (exactly 1), 0..1 (zero or one), 0..* (zero or many),
                   1..2 (exactly one or two)
    Type:          String(N), String(CLOB), Long(N), Date, DateTime,
                   Boolean(5), Grouping
    Meaning:       brief description of what the value represents and source

  EXAMPLE PATIENT
  =================
  Mdm Tan Mei Ling — Singapore citizen, Chinese, female, married, Buddhist,
  Mandarin-speaking. Came in for a cardiology follow-up with Dr Ruth Kam at
  Heart Clinic main branch on 4 May 2026.
================================================================================
-->

<putEvent xmlns="http://www.synapxe.sg/nehr/putEvent">  <!-- [M] card 1 Grouping | XML root, one per message -->


  <!-- ============================================================ -->
  <!-- CONTROL HEADER — every message includes this                  -->
  <!-- ============================================================ -->
