<!--
================================================================================
  HOW TO USE THIS REFERENCE
================================================================================

  1) STRUCTURE READING
     Read top to bottom. Element ORDER is what the spec defines and what XSD
     validation enforces — preserve it when constructing real messages.

  2) ANNOTATION DECODE
     <element>VALUE</element>  <! [M] card 1 String(50) | meaning >
                                  ↑    ↑     ↑          ↑
                                  Sig  Card  Type/Len   What/Source

     Significance: M / O / C
       M = Mandatory (must populate)
       O = Optional (populate if available; otherwise OMIT entirely)
       C = Conditional Mandatory (mandatory when condition holds)

     Cardinality: how many times the element can appear
       1     = exactly once
       0..1  = zero or one
       0..*  = zero or many
       1..2  = exactly one or two

     Type/Length: data type with max length
       String(N), String(CLOB), Long(N), Date, DateTime, Boolean(5), Grouping

  3) SIGNIFICANCE-PRECEDENCE RULE
     A Mandatory child within an Optional parent is Mandatory only IF the parent
     is included. If you skip the parent, you skip the child too.

       Optional parent:  <address>, <phone>, <referringClinician>, <nextOfKin>
       Inside them, Mandatory children become required ONLY if you include the parent.

  4) NO EMPTY TAGS RULE
     Per Synapxe Guide v0.42 (page 10):
       Source must EXCLUDE empty XML tags. Do not emit:
         ❌ <tag></tag>
         ❌ <tag/>
         ❌ <tag>NA</tag>  (unless NA is a meaning-bearing codeset value)
       If a value is missing or null, OMIT the entire element.

  5) FOR HEART CLINIC SPECIFICALLY
     - patientType.code = "O" (always)
     - eventType.code = "4" (always)
     - movementType.code = "1" (always, Visit_Type_(NEHR))
     - serviceSpecialty.code = "NEHR_SS_0002" (Cardiology, hardcode)
     - srcInstitution = "9403258" (main branch HCI; Farrer TBC)
     - srcApplication = "MDX-GCMS"
     - licenseeNumber = "L/9403258/MDS/007/242"
     - DO NOT emit admittingClinician, dischargingClinician, dischargeInformation
       (those are for inpatient encounters only)

  6) NHDD CODESETS
     Patient demographics use NHDD codes. The values shown above come from
     the sample JSON files in skills/nehr-data-mapping/references/nhdd-samples/.
     NB: these JSON values may differ from the spec's published sample values.
     Confirm with client before production transmission.

  7) SYNAPXE CODESETS
     Visit/event codings (patientType, eventType, movementType, serviceSpecialty)
     come from INT_2_1_Onboarding_CodeSetInventory_v2.29 (in workspace root).

  8) RUNNING THIS FILE
     This file is for reading, not for sending. It mixes outpatient and
     inpatient elements which would be invalid in any single transmission.
     For real transmissions: see NEHR_putEvent_Sample_Heart_Clinic.xml.

================================================================================
  MESSAGE TYPE VARIATIONS
================================================================================
  Clinical          : controlHeader + patient + event. msgType=Clinical.
  Administrative    : controlHeader + patient (NO event). msgType=Administrative.
  Cancel            : controlHeader + patient (NO event). msgType=Cancel.
  Merge             : controlHeader + patient WITH patientMergeType. msgType=Merge.

  → For Merge: include <patientMergeType>OBSOLETE</patientMergeType> in the
    obsolete patient's identification block, and submit a second message with
    <patientMergeType>SURVIVOR</patientMergeType> for the survivor.

================================================================================
-->
